11873	{"artifactId":"LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s3","entry":{"id":"migrated-LLD-315d510cb28100e2-s3-review","actor":{"id":"insrc:daemon","kind":"agent","properties":{}},"timestamp":"2026-10-17T14:58:25.224Z","operation":"review","outcome":{"result":"block","summary":"review: block","data":{"kind":"review","report":{"artifact":"design.story","stage":"design.story","verdict":"block","findings":[{"claimId":"coverage-of-intent.1","ref":"coverage-of-intent","item":"coverage-of-intent","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed fields and read-only sign-in interpretation cover s3's upstream intent, including the accepted deferral of field consumers.","evidence":"DEF ac10–ac14 require equivalent tracker settings across clients, remote target resolution, cross-client persistence and read-only policy. docs/plans/team-workflow.md explicitly records: 'sign-in is shown as a live read-only status' and 'ghPath, ghHost and branchPattern are stored and shown only'. The design follows that recorded decision. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, docs/plans/team-workflow.md]","action":"Retain the 'saved; not used yet' notes and the distinction between sign-in status and editable host configuration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.1","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The current resolver ignores a default entry's target, preserves explicit per-repo targets, and defaults to no tracker.","evidence":"resolveGithubConfig passes allowEntryTarget=true for the own entry and false for the default. resolveEntry uses gitOriginOwnerRepo when type is github without an eligible target. The final fallback is { type: 'none', source: 'default-config' }. [files: src/workflow/config/github.ts, src/workflow/config/__tests__/github.test.ts]","action":"Preserve these branches verbatim during the snapshot-resolver extraction.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"current-behaviour.2","ref":"current-behaviour","item":"current-behaviour","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Tracker setup currently writes the five stated configuration fields directly from the terminal process.","evidence":"ensureConfig writes { type: 'github', owner: remote.owner, repo: remote.repo, pushTasks: true, commitArtifacts: true } using writeFileSync. The terminal service directly returns runTrackerSetup(repoPath, opts). The setup test asserts that exact stored entry. [files: src/workflow/tracker/setup.ts, src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/setup.test.ts]","action":"Route the production terminal call through the proposed daemon seam while retaining the existing report formatting.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.1","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The existing GitHub adapter supports the proposed read-only identity lookup with the stated failure kinds.","evidence":"createGithubTracker(owner, repo) returns TrackerPort. Its whoAmI calls ghCurrentLogin only, maps an empty-login error to missing-signin, and maps GhCommandError through failure(). PortFailureKind is exactly missing-tool | missing-signin | unreachable | rejected. [files: src/workflow/tracker/github-adapter.ts, src/workflow/tracker/port.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts]","action":"Reuse whoAmI directly; do not introduce a second identity implementation.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"new-versus-reuse.2","ref":"new-versus-reuse","item":"new-versus-reuse","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The shared catalog is an existing pure assembly seam suitable for adding static repo field definitions.","evidence":"buildSettingsCatalog reads CONFIG_CATALOG, reasoningRoleTaxonomy and its rawConfig argument, then returns { options, groups, roles, tierNames, values }. It performs no file or tracker access. The current payload has no repoFields member. [files: src/config/settings-catalog.ts]","action":"Keep repository reads and live status out of buildSettingsCatalog.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.1","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The asynchronous trackerSetup migration identifies its current production caller chain.","evidence":"The production service wrapper calls runTrackerSetup; Services declares a synchronous TrackerSetupReport; command.ts immediately reads report.steps; ReposPane passes the synchronous result to setReport inside a deferred callback. These are all included in the design's migration inventory. Other imported engine calls found in the source search are setup tests. [files: src/cli/services/workflow.ts, src/cli/services/index.ts, src/cli/command.ts, src/cli/panes/ReposPane.tsx]","action":"Make the command helper and deferred TUI callback async, preserving their error handling.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"change-sites.2","ref":"change-sites","item":"change-sites","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed client changes target the actual catalog, rendering and write seams.","evidence":"VS Code's gateway currently returns { values }; extension.ts injects registeredRepos/rawConfig and the consent-gated writeKeyPath sink into repo-config. JetBrains loads settings on executeOnPooledThread and renders on invokeLater; PerRepoSection applies writes through writeSetting/clearSetting. Searches confirm the three named ConfigGateway fake classes and four named DaemonGateway test doubles. [files: vscode-plugin/src/config/gateway.ts, vscode-plugin/src/config/types.ts, vscode-plugin/src/extension.ts, vscode-plugin/src/panels/repo-config.ts, jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/settings/InsrcSettingsConfigurable.kt, jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/settings/PerRepoSection.kt, jetbrains-plugin/src/main/kotlin/ai/insors/insrc/jetbrains/daemon/DaemonGateway.kt]","action":"Update these seams and fixtures together with the interface additions.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.1","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Separating strict settings reads from the existing lenient resolver is necessary to preserve malformed-record behavior.","evidence":"loadGithubConfigFile catches read/parse failures and rejects null or primitive top levels, but does not validate nested entries. resolveGithubConfig tests entries against undefined, and resolveEntry immediately reads entry.type; a null own/default entry therefore throws. The design explicitly preserves that legacy path while validating settings snapshots separately. [files: src/workflow/config/github.ts, src/workflow/config/__tests__/github.test.ts]","action":"Retain characterization tests for null nested entries and loader-rejected inputs; do not silently route legacy callers through the strict reader.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"data-compatibility.2","ref":"data-compatibility","item":"data-compatibility","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Using the exact registered path as the settings key matches current registry and resolver identity.","evidence":"validateRepoPathShape applies path.resolve; addRepo stores that normalized path. Registry lookup compares row.path === path, without realpath resolution. The tracker resolver indexes file.repos?.[repoPath] directly. [files: src/db/repos.ts, src/workflow/config/github.ts]","action":"Use listRepos' registered strings and preserve separate entries for separately registered symlink paths.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"boundaries.1","ref":"boundaries","item":"boundaries","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The design consumes the implemented policy contract without redesigning policy ownership or persistence.","evidence":"TeamPolicy contains the six named rule fields and source.ref/source.fetchedAt. policyReader has the stated PolicyResult<TeamPolicy | 'none'> shape. readUnseen may acquire the sighting lock and publish first-sighting metadata. The design permits that existing behavior and introduces no policy writer. Its additional sc1 dependency is explicitly acknowledged, although the HLD still says 's3 needs only sc2'. [files: src/workflow/team/types.ts, src/workflow/team/policy-reader.ts, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md]","action":"Synchronize the upstream dependency inventory to include sc1; keep policy and sighting implementation owned by s2.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.1","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"The proposed timeout and early-close handling addresses actual unresolved-promise paths in rpc.","evidence":"rpc currently registers connect, data and error handlers only. It has no deadline and no end/close rejection, so a silent peer or a peer closing without a response can leave the promise pending. The proposed opt-in handling covers those paths. [files: src/shared/ipc-client.ts]","action":"Test silent, end-before-response and close-before-response sockets, including timer cleanup and single settlement.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"},{"claimId":"error-paths.2","ref":"error-paths","item":"error-paths","kind":"semantic","severity":"MED","premise":"The 15-second daemon request deadline means the entire tracker setup finishes within that deadline.","evidence":"The design says 'Setup finishes within the deadline'. However, runTrackerSetup subsequently executes auth, scopes, labels, issue types and optional project operations synchronously. ensureLabels contains 'for (const label of SETUP_LABELS)', and each migrated label command can consume its own 10-second timeout. The existing test explicitly verifies that setup continues after a label timeout. Bounding the preceding config RPC cannot bound the entire report-producing operation. [files: src/workflow/tracker/setup.ts, src/workflow/tracker/github.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/setup.test.ts, src/cli/panes/ReposPane.tsx, src/cli/command.ts]","action":"State that the deadline bounds only the config RPC. Scope timeout assertions to that phase and separately assert that remaining setup steps execute; do not promise a 15-second total setup duration.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"does-not-hold"},{"claimId":"tests.1","ref":"tests","item":"tests","kind":"semantic","severity":"LOW","premise":"Each acceptance criterion assigned to s3 has a proposed proving test grounded in the existing implementation seams.","evidence":"The upstream assigns ac10–ac14 to s3. Section 6 maps them respectively to IDE editing/status, terminal parity, remote-target resolution, persistence across clients, and read-only policy/refusal tests. Existing resolver tests pin target behavior, setup tests expose _setTrackerExecForTests, and the VS Code seam test explicitly enumerates allowed gateway IPC methods, matching the proposed test updates. This verifies test-plan coverage, not execution or implementation of the new tests. [files: docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/DEF.md, docs/epics/team-signoff-claim-based-workflow-E20261016315d510c/HLD.md, src/workflow/config/__tests__/github.test.ts, src/workflow/tracker/__tests__/setup.test.ts, vscode-plugin/src/config/__tests__/seam.test.ts]","action":"Implement the mapped tests, with the timeout assertion narrowed as described above.","fixability":"manual","outcome":"holds"}],"counts":{"high":0,"med":1,"low":12,"unverified":0},"template":"design-spec","reviewedAt":"2026-10-17T14:58:25.224Z","model":"cli-codex:gpt-6-astra","reviewedBy":"daemon"},"resolutions":{}}}}}
